{"id":"a7d2f45c-c8fa-4be8-8b74-63b41ab8dcbd","name":"Why MCP is awesome: content at the speed of thought","path":"WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome: content at the speed of thought","docTypeId":"7189041a-69ca-47ff-892a-e367366eb4a5","templateId":"ee187aa9-feed-41aa-8877-8f2041acc9a2","state":"PublishedPendingChanges","domains":[],"values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextArea","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"excerpt","value":"From an empty database to a published blog in one sitting. A look at what happens when your CMS speaks MCP."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.MediaPicker3","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"featuredImage","value":[{"key":"3fafa912-3d76-4b3d-9d87-8a7d29308175","mediaKey":"7947d22c-5847-43aa-a9f8-b31f40b9b96c","mediaTypeAlias":"Image","crops":[],"focalPoint":null}]},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.DateTime","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"publishedDate","value":"2026-10-09 00:00:00"},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.BlockGrid","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"body","value":{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"0f1fcf8f-3ee5-4f3e-b7f0-b1cb6c52ceb7","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"1fbaa504-f0ce-433f-8c13-59b73a24576e","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"80e21fa5-2f4c-431d-889d-802ab11263ae","settingsKey":null}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c","key":"68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"body","value":{"markup":"<p>This entire blog — the schema, the pages, the images, the publishing — was created by an AI agent talking to Umbraco over the Model Context Protocol. No human clicked a single button in the backoffice.</p><p>That is the headline, but the interesting part is what it felt like: modeling content, writing posts and shipping them became one continuous conversation instead of three separate tools glued together with copy-paste.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"3406fa98-72a3-4298-b06b-497c4d882f28","key":"0f1fcf8f-3ee5-4f3e-b7f0-b1cb6c52ceb7","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.MediaPicker3","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"image","value":[{"key":"c444b5e3-5884-4c5e-b148-dc1f2db15ea1","mediaKey":"8f1c0f11-7f95-4cd1-95cf-0bbc51015bcd","mediaTypeAlias":"Image","crops":[],"focalPoint":null}]},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"caption","value":"A circuit board with standardised connections — photo by Alexandre Debiève on Unsplash"}]},{"contentTypeKey":"976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c","key":"1fbaa504-f0ce-433f-8c13-59b73a24576e","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"body","value":{"markup":"<p>MCP turns the CMS into a first-class citizen of the agent's world. The agent can discover what content types exist, understand their properties, and then act with confidence — creating, updating and publishing through the same management API the backoffice uses.</p><p>The result is a workflow where the distance between an idea and a published page is measured in sentences, not in tickets.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"2130109b-aa66-44b2-b932-b19b0d045d73","key":"80e21fa5-2f4c-431d-889d-802ab11263ae","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextArea","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"quote","value":"The best tool interface is the one the model already knows how to use."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"attribution","value":"Why MCP wins for content operations"}]}],"settingsData":[],"expose":[{"contentKey":"68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"0f1fcf8f-3ee5-4f3e-b7f0-b1cb6c52ceb7","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"1fbaa504-f0ce-433f-8c13-59b73a24576e","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"80e21fa5-2f4c-431d-889d-802ab11263ae","culture":null,"segment":null}]}}],"urls":["/why-mcp-is-awesome-content-at-the-speed-of-thought/"],"docType":"blogPost","template":"BlogPost"}
